 "pod": "embg2-ab11 on gpuworker01 for the tests and the HTTP rows, and embg2-ab12 on gpuworker01 for the separate-streams run.  Each was the only GPU pod on the node.",
 "method": "Each build ran its nine EmbeddingGemma 2 GPU test binaries, then four HTTP passes in the order base, batch, batch, base, base, batch, batch, base, with a new server for each pass and 60 requests per row per pass.  Each value is the mean of the four passes' medians or p95s, and the speedup is the base median divided by the batch median.  The text rows come from tools/models/embedding_gemma2/http_bench.py, including the 16 x 1 x 16 row.  The image rows send one 320 x 180 PNG followed by a newline in the typed content format, 269 tokens, at 1, 4, and 16 clients.  The mixed row has 16 client threads that take 120 requests alternating an image request and a 16-word text request, so each kind has 60 requests per pass.  The first server of each build also ran tests/functional/embeddings.py and tests/functional/embedding_images.py, and all passed.  The separate_streams entries come from embg2-ab12, which ran the same builds in the same order for four passes each.  In each pass 8 threads sent 8 image requests each while 8 other threads sent 16-word text requests until the image threads finished, so the text request count differs between passes.  Each separate_streams value is the mean of the four passes' values.  The embg2-ab12 image holds the same two gufo store paths and differs only in its entry script.",
